{"uid": "mfg-2103-14-02", "question_type": "explanatory", "question_subtype": "shortfall_cause", "raw_text": "Based on my analysis of Plant 2103, Period 14 data:\n\nOn day 187, for POV500M24P:\n- Stock at start of day: 0 units\n- Production: 10 units\n- Available for dispatch: 10 units\n- Older backorders carried forward: 1099 units (from days 185-186)\n- New order placed: 2615 units\n- Total demand: 3714 units\n- Shipped: 10 units (all to older backorders per \"oldest first\" policy)\n- The day 187 order received 0 units shipped\n\nEvaluating each choice as a responsible condition (would the order have shipped in full without this condition):\n\n- **Choice 0**: If production on day 187 had been \u2265 2615 (negating \"production < order\"), with 2615 available, 1099 would serve the old backorder, leaving only 1516 for the new order. Not full. **Not responsible.**\n\n- **Choice 1**: If older backorders had not been served first, the new order would have been served first with 10 units available. Only 10 of 2615 would ship. Not full. **Not responsible.**\n\n- **Choice 2**: If there had been enough stock (i.e., stock \u2265 ~3704 units so available \u2265 3714), all 1099 old backorders plus the full 2615 new order would have been served. The order would have shipped in full. **Responsible.**\n\n- **Choice 3**: If production on day 186 had been \u2265 1033, old backorders might be reduced or cleared, but day 187 production is still only 10 units. With 10 available and 2615 ordered, the new order still wouldn't ship in full. **Not responsible.**\n\n```json\n{\"choices\": {\"0\": false, \"1\": false, \"2\": true, \"3\": false}}\n```", "parsed": {"choices": {"0": false, "1": false, "2": true, "3": false}}, "score": {"question_correct": true, "options_correct": 4, "options_total": 4}, "usage": {"input_tokens": 154167, "cached_input_tokens": 0, "output_tokens": 30630, "reasoning_tokens": 29920, "llm_calls": 0, "total_tokens": 184797}, "latency_s": 504.8, "trace": {"finish_r